    "md5": "8404f5dd395cedc427da134e70dff5c9",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1545,
    "chunk_text": "One day, we managed to impress a fine lady from Gl\u00fccksburg-Holnis, in Northern Germany. She was Dora. She took us both in her hand, set us on her palm carefully, and gazed at us sharply, studying how we looked. We heard her say to her husband Wilhelm that we both looked so cute. So they picked us from the shop, brought us home, and placed us on Dora\u2019s piano. We kept enjoying to the beautiful melodies she played on the piano, and had a jolly time, listening to the always theatrical conversations that took place with different personalities in their drawing room. Gamini was there in August 1990, and when he was leaving, along with many other toys, we were both given to him, as he and his wife Dammi had two small boys called Nivanka and Danilo. We were again safely packed in a brown paper bag and kept in Gamini\u2019s luggage until we were taken out on his return home.\n\nFrom July to November 2025, the house underwent an overall restoration. It started with the replacement of the ceiling with a new one, and went on to the re-plastering of the walls and polishing the doors and windows, and ended up painting the floor with titanium. Because of the dust getting accumulated every day, Gamini and Dammi spent the night in a different house that belongs to them. The house was in the care of some total strangers. The furniture was being dismantled and placed in the back of the house. The small objects were packed and put in different places. The curios among which we used to be kept were put in boxes and taken to a different place."
  },
