    "chunk_size_bytes": 1960,
    "chunk_text": "From July to November 2025, the house underwent an overall restoration. It started with the replacement of the ceiling with a new one, and went on to the re-plastering of the walls and polishing the doors and windows, and ended up painting the floor with titanium. Because of the dust getting accumulated every day, Gamini and Dammi spent the night in a different house that belongs to them. The house was in the care of some total strangers. The furniture was being dismantled and placed in the back of the house. The small objects were packed and put in different places. The curios among which we used to be kept were put in boxes and taken to a different place.\n\nDuring the Cyclonic Storm Ditwah of Nov-Dec 2025 that lasted over a week, there were heavy showers from morning till evening. Stuck among the reeds of grass on a mound, I remained scared of being either dashed away in a torrent of water or buried under a heap of mud. I really felt my inability to get hold of anything during the floating, or walk into a safe place, or make a cry for help. I felt I was just a lump of plastic without any power at all. While wondering what I should do, I once heard Gamini telling Dammi that I was missing. I realised then that my mother is still safe inside the house. Then I felt the sorrow she would suffer in my absence. She has her legs always stretched out to keep me on her lap. Without me there, in her usual posture with her legs outstretched, she looks empty. That means without me, she has no value. We depend on each other to fulfil the meaning of our existence.\n\nDay by day the weather improved. There were periods of sunshine every day. The torrential showers stopped. The ground became a little solid once again. I see Gamini and Dammi moving around. Yet I had no way of telling them about my presence or clinging on to them asking for help. I have thus spent nearly five months in the open air. I was wondering how long I would last like this."
  },
