    "chunk_size_bytes": 1770,
    "chunk_text": "Day by day the weather improved. There were periods of sunshine every day. The torrential showers stopped. The ground became a little solid once again. I see Gamini and Dammi moving around. Yet I had no way of telling them about my presence or clinging on to them asking for help. I have thus spent nearly five months in the open air. I was wondering how long I would last like this.\n\nExcited by what was going on, I remember Gamini coming out and studying what had been found. He recognised me immediately and brought my mother to you. He carefully placed me on my mother\u2019s lap. So we could sit together and make a show of mother and son love. I was highly pampered in my mother\u2019s lap, a luxury I had missed for a long time. Because of your excitement, you happened to drop me on the ground once again. Then I was so upset, but your very kind mother found me again, and fitted me in my place.\n\nIt was good that your mother decided to release us only once you all have arrived home. So, in a few minutes, you all took leave of my former guardians Gamini and Dammi, and moved to my present dwelling at Weligalle. I am happy again with my mother in the care of you and your family at this beautiful home. Meth, please make sure that I always keep sitting on the lap of my mother. That is the only joy I have in life. Thank you.\n\n(The writer of this story holds a BA (Kelaniya), MA (Edinburgh), PhD (Vaasa), FRSA, is Professor Emeritus of English, Department of English & Linguistics, University of Ruhuna)\n\nQuitting the UNP and battling in the Supreme Court to save our seats\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
