    "chunk_size_bytes": 1644,
    "chunk_text": "New model pre-school vested in Medadumbara to boost early childhood education\n\nJohn Keells Foundation (JKF) and Victoria Golf Resort have formally vested the newly constructed Nithulemada Model Pre-School to the Medadumbara Pradeshiya Sabha. The facility aims to provide critical early childhood education to children aged 3-5 years in the Kandy District, addressing a two-decade-long need for a permanent space.\n\nThe project, initiated in 2020 under JKF\u2019s \u2018Praja Shakthi\u2019 community empowerment initiative, overcame delays from the pandemic and economic challenges to complete construction in October 2025. The vesting ceremony was attended by Minister K.D. Lalkantha, provincial officials, and JKF representatives.\n\nSpeaking at the event, JKF Head of CSR Carmeline Jayasuriya highlighted the dual focus on equitable education and fostering social cohesion. \u201cWe aim to create learning environments that encourage understanding, respect, and unity among children and communities,\u201d she said.\n\nMinister Lalkantha emphasized the foundational importance of early childhood development. \u201cIf we truly want to change, we must begin at the very foundation,\u201d he stated, praising the school as a potential model for future government preschools.\n\nThe event featured performances by preschool children and a demonstration by students from JKF\u2019s English scholarship programme, showcasing the foundation\u2019s broader educational impact in the region.\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
