    "chunk_size_bytes": 1371,
    "chunk_text": "MSTI Maritime Academy inaugurates Sri Lanka\u2019s most advanced Full Mission Bridge Simulator\n\nPorts and Civil Aviation Deputy Minister Janitha Ruwan Kodithuwakku (right) and MSTI Chairman Captain Ajith Peiris\n\nFrom left: MSTI Head of Operations Captain Anura Herath, Chairman Captain Ajith Peiris, Ports and Civil Aviation Deputy Minister Janitha Ruwan Kodithuwakku, and MSTI Head of Engineering Gihan Venturi\n\nMSTI Maritime Academy, established in 1986 as Sri Lanka\u2019s first privately owned maritime training school, has developed a distinguished legacy of over three decades in producing globally competent seafarers. With modern training facilities located in Dehiwala, Katukurunda, and Kalutara, and a faculty composed of Master Mariners and Chief Engineers, MSTI continues to set benchmarks for high-quality, industry-relevant maritime education.\n\nToday, MSTI Maritime Academy celebrated a significant milestone with the inauguration of its state-of-the-art Full Mission Bridge Simulator, the most advanced maritime bridge simulator currently available in Sri Lanka.\n\nThe ceremony was attended by the Chief Guest, Deputy Minister of Ports and Civil Aviation Janitha Ruwan Kodithuwakku, along with MSTI Chairman Captain Ajith Peiris, senior officials from the maritime and port sectors, industry partners, maritime professionals, academics, and media representatives."
